This file states, against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti, the headlines of `README.md` that
carry a Lean name, each with every conclusion the README attaches to it. It is not an exhaustive
acceptance test: the other headlines of the README are targets of the same standing, stated in
prose. Discharging this file finishes neither a layer nor the roadmap.

Headlines of the README without a Lean statement here because they need something this file does
not have, and what each lacks:
- the 192 automorphisms (README 2.3) need the group generated by the transformations of 2.1–2.2
  as a group of pairs (prefactor, Möbius map), which the README describes but does not name;
- the Weierstrass form (README 2.4) needs branches of `(℘(ξ) − e_j)^{s}` along paths;
- the connection coefficients (README 3.5) need the solutions at `1` continued along `(0, 1)`
  as named functions of `q`;
- the continued fraction for the eigenvalues (README 5.3) and the hypergeometric and Jacobi
  expansions (README 5.4) need the continued fractions and minimal solutions of
  SpecialFunctionsEiLiErfIncompleteGamma 4.1, which this file does not copy, and the families
